        "# **Uber Supply-Demand Gap Analysis**\n",
        "\n",
        "##### **Project Type** - EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis)\n",
        "\n",
        "##### **Name -** *BURADA TRISHA*\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# **Project Summary**\n",
        "\n",
        "This project performs an Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on Uber ride request data collected over 5 days (July 11–15, 2016). The dataset contains 6,745 ride requests between the city and the airport. The main objective is to identify the root causes of the supply-demand gap — situations where riders request a cab but either no cars are available or the driver cancels the trip.\n",
        "\n",
        "Key findings from this analysis:\n",
        "- **Night time (7 PM–10 PM)** has the highest number of unfulfilled requests, primarily from the **Airport** side due to \"No Cars Available.\"\n",
        "- **Morning and Early Morning (12 AM–10 AM)** see the highest driver **cancellations**, mostly from the **City** side, as drivers don't want to make the long airport trip early in the day.\n",
        "- The supply-demand gap is significantly larger at the **Airport** (≈1000 unfulfilled requests) compared to the **City** (≈820).\n",
        "- **Recommended solutions**: Incentivize drivers with surge/rush-hour pricing during morning slots; introduce dedicated night-shift drivers to cover the airport-to-city demand at night.\n",
        "\n",
        "# **GitHub Link**\n",
        "[https://github.com/yourusername/uber-eda-project](https://github.com/yourusername/uber-eda-project)\n",
        "\n",
        "# **Problem Statement**\n",
        "Uber is facing a significant supply-demand gap: many ride requests are going unfulfilled either because no cabs are available or because drivers are cancelling rides. This hurts customer experience and revenue.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### **Define Your Business Objective**\n",
        "To identify **when** (time of day) and **where** (pickup point: City or Airport) the gap is most severe, understand the **root causes** (cancellations vs. unavailability), and recommend **data-driven solutions** to bridge the gap.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "# ***Let's Begin!***"
      ],
      "id": "cPFaEjkFOBJr"
    },
